# Beacon Dashboards — full build spec

Two web apps in one pnpm workspace. Read `00-beacon-shared.mdc` first. The API contracts are in `10-edge.mdc` §8 and §10 (ship) and `20-shore.mdc` §8 (shore). **Use those exact paths and field names.**

| App | Users | Hosted | API |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ship-web` | Master, Safety Officer, on the bridge PC or a tablet | Built to `dist/` and served by the **edge server at `/`** (same origin) | `/api/v1` on the edge |
| `shore-web` | Fleet safety team, psychology team, admin | **Firebase Hosting** (`byf-beacon-2026.web.app`) | `VITE_API_BASE` = Cloud Run `shore-api` URL |

## 1. Stack
- pnpm workspace: `dashboards/packages/ui` (shared tokens + components), `dashboards/ship-web`, `dashboards/shore-web`
- React 18, TypeScript strict, Vite, React Router, **TanStack Query** (polling + caching), Zod for runtime validation of API responses
- Styling: CSS variables + CSS modules (or Tailwind with local build; **no CDN**). Charts: **Recharts** (bundled). QR: `qrcode` npm (render to canvas). Icons: `lucide-react`.
- Fonts **self-hosted** via `@fontsource/barlow`, `@fontsource/barlow-condensed`, `@fontsource/jetbrains-mono`: `ship-web` must work with no internet, so nothing may load from a CDN.
- **MSW (Mock Service Worker)** with fixtures for both apps (`VITE_MOCK=1`) so the UI can be built before the backends are ready. Fixtures = the example JSON in the specs, including the crane cluster scenario.
- shore-web auth: Firebase JS SDK (`firebase/auth`) with email/password; attach the ID token as `Authorization: Bearer`; refresh on 401.
- ship-web auth: `POST /api/v1/auth/login {username, pin}` → JWT kept in memory + `sessionStorage`; auto-logout after 12 h or a 401.

## 2. Visual design (shared `packages/ui`)
An operations console for people on a ship's bridge and in a fleet office: calm, dense, readable at a glance, no decoration.
- Tokens (light + dark, follow `prefers-color-scheme` plus a toggle):
  - ink `#14202E` / `#E3E9F0`, ground `#F3F5F8` / `#0D141C`, panel `#FFFFFF` / `#16212D`, line `#C9D1DB` / `#34465A`, muted `#586777` / `#93A2B3`
  - accent **BYF signal yellow** `#A86F00` on light / `#F2B530` on dark (primary actions, the sync link, the brief's recommended action)
  - severity: low `#3B7D4F`, medium `#B7791F`, high `#C2410C`, critical `#B91C1C` (pills with text, never colour alone)
  - privacy teal `#0F766E` / `#5EC4B6` (k-anon notices, "hidden for privacy")
- Type: Barlow Condensed for headings and big numbers, Barlow for body, JetBrains Mono for IDs, timestamps and sizes. `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` on all numbers.
- Components: `AppShell` (left nav, top bar with vessel/fleet name + link status), `StatTile`, `SeverityPill`, `StatusPill`, `LinkStatus`, `DataTable` (sortable, sticky header, keyboard row focus), `Drawer`, `EmptyState`, `PrivacyNote`, `LanguageTag` (e.g. `HI`), `RelativeTime`, `Sparkline`, `ConfirmBar`.
- Layout: works from 1024 px (tablet landscape) up to 1920 px; the main overview fits one screen at 1366×768 without scrolling.
- Never show `reporter_ref` (the APIs don't return it; don't add it).

## 3. ship-web (Master / Safety Officer)

Polling: overview, near-misses and sync status every **5 s** (TanStack Query `refetchInterval`); everything else 30 s. Show a thin "Updated 3 s ago" label.

### 3.1 Login
Username + 4–6 digit PIN, large inputs. Vessel name from `GET /api/v1/health` (unauthenticated) is shown on the login screen.

### 3.2 Overview (`/`) — the demo screen
- Top bar: vessel name, **LinkStatus** (`VSAT up · last sync 2 min ago` / `VSAT down · 5 items waiting`), Gemma model status.
- Red banner when `medical_alerts_open > 0` → link to Medical alerts.
- Yellow banner for unread fleet alerts: "**Fleet alert:** Recurring crane hydraulic leaks on 3 vessels. Matches a past accident (fractured wrist)." → opens the alert.
- StatTiles: Reports (24 h) · Open hazards · High/critical open · Check-ins today · Crew paired.
- **Today's brief** card (from `/ship/brief/today`): source badge `On-board AI` or `Shore-enriched`; the **recommended action** in large text with its "why" and evidence links (open the cited reports); rest-compliance and crew-trend rows (crew trend shows "Hidden: fewer than 5 check-ins" when `k_anonymity_ok=false`). Button: Regenerate.
- **Recent reports** (latest 6): severity pill, area · hazard, one-line description, language tag, "repeat" badge if `recurring`, "2 similar on board" if `similar_onboard > 0`, photo icon, time. Click → detail drawer.
- **Sync panel**: last delta size in mono ("1.1 KB"), pending counts, **Sync now** (`POST /sync/run`, button shows a spinner), and a demo switch **"Simulate VSAT down"** (`POST /sync/link`). Animate the pending count decreasing after a sync.

### 3.3 Near-misses (`/near-misses`)
- Filters: status, severity, area, hazard type, date range, "repeat only". DataTable columns: time, severity, area (+ detail), hazard, description, language, rank group, status, shared-with-shore icon.
- Detail drawer: AI summary fields; **What the crew member said** (original text, language tag) and English translation side by side; photos (click to enlarge); clarification Q&A; "Similar on this ship" list; AI extraction confidence (small, mono).
- **Assign action** form: action text (English; crew see it translated), owner rank (select), due date, status → `PATCH`. Show "Crew will see this in their language".
- Close with a closing note (status `closed`).

### 3.4 Crew wellbeing (`/wellbeing`)
- Persistent PrivacyNote at top: "You see groups of 5 or more people only. Individual check-ins are never shown. Conversations stay on crew phones."
- 14-day line chart for mood, fatigue and workload; suppressed days drawn as gaps with a hatched band and tooltip "Fewer than 5 check-ins: hidden for privacy".
- Bars by rank group (suppressed groups shown as a grey "hidden" bar label, no value).
- Themes as a simple ranked list with counts.
- No drill-down, no export of individual data, no per-person anything.

### 3.5 Notices (`/notices`)
- Composer: title, body (English), priority (normal/urgent). Preview text: "Will be translated into Hindi and Tagalog for 14 crew devices". Send → `POST /ship/notices`.
- List: priority, title, created, source (ship/shore), acks `7/14` as a small bar.

### 3.6 Pair crew phones (`/pairing`)
- Big QR from `qr_payload` (JSON stringified), the join code in large mono below it, expiry, paired devices count, **Rotate code** button. Instructions: "Open Beacon on your phone → Scan the ship code". Also a full-screen "Show on screen" mode for crew to scan from a distance.

### 3.7 Ask the manuals (`/ask`)
- Chat-like Q&A over the ship's SMS documents (`POST /ship/ask`). Answers show citation chips (doc title + page). If `grounded=false`, show the refusal plainly.
- Documents tab: upload (.pdf/.md/.txt) → `POST /ship/docs`, list with chunk counts.

### 3.8 Fleet alerts (`/fleet-alerts`) and Medical alerts (`/medical`)
- Fleet alerts: list + detail (title, body, linked accident cases, received time), Mark read.
- Medical alerts: only category `medical`; rank group, time, Acknowledge. Clear guidance text: "A crew member reported a medical problem. Check on them now."

## 4. shore-web (fleet office)

Nav items depend on `role` from `GET /api/v1/me`: `shore_safety` and `admin` see Fleet, Clusters, Near-misses, Wellbeing, Reports, Ask, Corpus (+ Admin for admin); `shore_psych` sees **only** Escalations and Wellbeing. Route guards enforce this in the UI too (the API enforces it regardless).

Polling: overview and clusters every 10 s (the demo moment is the cluster appearing live).

### 4.1 Sign in
Firebase email/password. After sign-in show the role. No role → "Ask an admin to give you access".

### 4.2 Fleet overview (`/`)
- Headline banner for `top_cluster`: "**Active cluster** · Recurring crane hydraulic leaks · 3 vessels · High" → cluster detail. Animate it in when it first appears (respect `prefers-reduced-motion`).
- StatTiles: Vessels online · Near-misses (7 d) · High open · Active clusters.
- Vessel table: name, online dot + "last sync 4 min ago", near-misses 7 d (sparkline), high open, active clusters, wellbeing trend arrow or "hidden" (k-anon). Click → vessel detail.

### 4.3 Clusters (`/clusters`, `/clusters/:id`) — the main shore demo screen
- List: title, hazard, area, vessels count, reports count, risk pill, last seen.
- Detail:
  - Timeline of member reports across vessels (vessel name, date, original-language tag, English description, severity, repeat badge). Click a report → drawer with original + translation + photos.
  - **Linked accident cases** cards: case id, outcome (e.g. "Serious injury"), summary, precursors with the overlapping ones highlighted (`explanation.precursor_overlap`), a `Synthetic` badge when `_synthetic`.
  - **Gemini explanation**: summary, why it matters, recommended actions; citation chips that scroll to and highlight the cited report/case.
  - **Send alert to vessels**: preview of the alert text, vessel checklist (defaults: cluster vessels + same-fleet vessels), optional note → `POST /fleet/clusters/{id}/alert`; then show "Delivered at next sync" status per vessel.

### 4.4 Near-misses explorer (`/near-misses`)
Filters (vessel, hazard, area, severity, dates), table, detail drawer with photos (signed URLs) and cluster link.

### 4.5 Vessel detail (`/vessels/:id`)
Header (name, fleet, online, last sync, edge version), recent near-misses, weekly wellbeing (suppressed weeks hatched), clusters and alerts for this vessel, **sync log** table (time, delta size in KB in mono, counts): this is the visual proof that the sync is tiny.

### 4.6 Wellbeing (`/wellbeing`)
Heatmap vessels × weeks for mood (and a toggle for fatigue/workload); suppressed cells hatched with the privacy tooltip. PrivacyNote explains k = 5.

### 4.7 Monthly report (`/reports`)
Month picker, rendered report (headline, sections in markdown, top risks linked to clusters, recommended actions), the numbers table from `data`, Regenerate. "Written by Gemini from the numbers shown" note.

### 4.8 Ask (`/ask`)
Natural-language questions → `POST /fleet/ask`; show the answer and a collapsible "How this was answered" listing the tool calls and arguments.

### 4.9 Escalations (`/escalations`, `shore_psych` only)
Queue sorted by created time; each item: vessel, category, contact channel, consented summary (if any), status. Actions: Mark contacted (with note), Resolve. Calm design; no red. A note: "These requests were made with the crew member's consent. Conversation transcripts are never shared."

### 4.10 Corpus (`/corpus`)
Search accident cases; upload a JSON list or paste raw report text (structured by Gemini) → show the structured result before saving.

### 4.11 Admin (`/admin`, admin only)
Create vessel → show the API key once with a copy button and a warning that it won't be shown again.

## 5. Project layout
```
dashboards/
├── package.json  pnpm-workspace.yaml  tsconfig.base.json
├── packages/ui/src/{tokens.css, components/*, charts/*, format.ts}
├── ship-web/
│   ├── vite.config.ts            # base "/", build.outDir "dist"; dev proxy /api → http://localhost:8080
│   └── src/{main.tsx, api/{client.ts, schemas.ts, hooks.ts}, mocks/{handlers.ts, fixtures/*.json}, routes/*, features/*}
└── shore-web/
    ├── vite.config.ts  firebase.json  .firebaserc  (project byf-beacon-2026, public: dist, SPA rewrite)
    └── src/{main.tsx, firebase.ts, api/*, mocks/*, routes/*, features/*}
```
`api/schemas.ts` has Zod schemas mirroring the spec responses; parse every response and show a clear error state ("The server sent something unexpected: field X") instead of crashing.

## 6. Build and deploy
- `pnpm --filter ship-web build` → copy `ship-web/dist` into the edge image (`SHIP_WEB_DIST`). Add this to the edge Makefile (`make web`).
- `pnpm --filter shore-web build && firebase deploy --only hosting --project byf-beacon-2026`.
- `.env.example` for shore-web: `VITE_API_BASE`, `VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY`, `VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN`, `VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID`, `VITE_MOCK`.

## 7. Quality bar
- Every screen has loading, empty and error states. Empty states say what will appear and how (e.g. "No reports yet. Crew can report from the Beacon app.").
- Keyboard: visible focus ring, tables navigable, drawers close on Esc.
- No network requests to anything other than the configured API (ship-web: same origin only). Add a test that scans `dist/` for `http://`/`https://` URLs other than `localhost` and fails if found (ship-web only).
- Playwright smoke test per app against MSW mocks: ship-web login → overview shows brief + fleet alert banner → assign an action. shore-web sign-in (mocked) → cluster banner → cluster detail shows 3 vessels and SYN-ACC-001 → send alert.

## 8. Build order
1. ⭐ **D1** Workspace, `packages/ui` tokens + AppShell + StatTile + pills + DataTable, MSW with fixtures for both apps.
2. ⭐ **D2** ship-web: login, Overview (brief, recent reports, sync panel + demo switch, banners), Pairing QR.
3. ⭐ **D3** shore-web: Firebase sign-in, Fleet overview with live cluster banner, Cluster detail + send alert, Vessel detail with sync log.
4. **D4** ship-web: Near-misses table + drawer + assign action, Wellbeing (k-anon visuals), Notices, Fleet/Medical alerts.
5. **D5** shore-web: Near-misses explorer, Wellbeing heatmap, Escalations (psych), Corpus, Admin.
6. **D6** Ask (both), Monthly report, dark mode pass, Playwright smoke tests, offline URL scan.
